+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes how members are reminded of a pickup, or is about to propose email reminders to save the SMS
+cost. The day before a pickup, larder texts the member that their pantry order is ready and when to collect it. The
+reminder goes by SMS, at about 40 euros a month, because a trial of email reminders in 2025 more than doubled the
+pantry orders nobody picked up, and their fresh food was thrown away.
+
+## Message
+
+The day before the pickup slot, `remind` in `larder/reminders.py` sends the member one message: "Your pantry order is
+ready for pickup {pickup}."
+
+## Channel
+
+The message goes by SMS to the member's phone. `CHANNEL` in `larder/reminders.py` selects it; the email branch
+beside it is the one the 2025 trial used.
+
+Email is free and SMS is not, so switching has been proposed several times; issue 52 was the third request in one
+year. It was tried: from April to June 2025 reminders went by email. The email provider reported that 34% of the
+reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup is a
+packed bag whose fresh food goes in the bin by closing time. Many members share one phone within a family and never
+check email, but they see a text. Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by
+August.
